## CLI Reference

```
radar scan <path-to-package.json> [OPTIONS]

Arguments:
  PATH  Path to the package.json file to scan  [required]

Options:
  --json PATH          Export results to a JSON file
  --no-cache           Skip the local cache and fetch fresh data
  --fail-under INT     Exit code 1 if any package scores below this threshold
  --help               Show this message and exit
```

```
radar version          Show the installed version
```

## Configuration

### GitHub Token

Set the `GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable to increase API rate limits (unauthenticated requests are limited to 60/hour):

```bash
export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
```

### Cache

API responses are cached locally for 24 hours in `~/.dependency-radar/cache/`. Use `--no-cache` to bypass.

## Development

```bash
# Install dev dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run the test suite
pytest -v

# Run just the scoring tests
pytest tests/test_scoring.py -v
```

## Project Structure

```
dependency-radar/
├── radar/
│   ├── __init__.py    # Data models (PackageInfo, NpmData, GitHubData, PackageHealth)
│   ├── cli.py         # Typer entry point (scan, version commands)
│   ├── parsers.py     # Parse package.json (dependencies + devDependencies)
│   ├── fetchers.py    # npm registry + GitHub API calls (concurrent)
│   ├── scoring.py     # Health score logic (pure functions)
│   ├── cache.py       # Local JSON cache with 24h expiry
│   └── report.py      # Rich table + JSON export
├── tests/
│   ├── test_parsers.py
│   └── test_scoring.py
├── README.md
└── pyproject.toml
```

